/* DISCOVERY / derivation: "predictive control is asymptotically wrong under confounding".
   The headline of CHC (notebook 01) hardened into a theorem. A controller that optimises the
   OBSERVATIONAL cost (effect fit from confounded logs) inherits a SYSTEMATIC bias (omitted-variable
   bias beta) that does NOT vanish with sample size, so its control regret is bounded below by a
   positive floor. A controller that optimises the INTERVENTIONAL cost (the causal effect) has zero
   regret. Maxima is the symbolic source of truth; verify before implementing. */
display2d : false$

/* ---- Part 1: the observational effect carries a fixed omitted-variable bias (population, no n) ---
   Confounded plant: z confounds -- u = alpha*z + nu,  x' = b*u + gamma*z.  The observational
   regression slope of x' on u is Cov(x',u)/Var(u); with E[nu]=E[z]=0, nu indep z: */
Cov_xu : b*(alpha^2*Vz + Vnu) + gamma*alpha*Vz$   /* Cov(x',u) = b*Var(u) + gamma*Cov(z,u) */
Var_u  : alpha^2*Vz + Vnu$
b_obs  : ratsimp(Cov_xu / Var_u)$                  /* observational (predictive) effect */
beta   : ratsimp(b_obs - b)$                       /* the systematic bias = b_obs - b_causal */
print("Part 1  b_obs =", b_obs)$
print("Part 1  OVB beta = b_obs - b =", beta, "  (a POPULATION constant: independent of n)")$

/* ---- Part 2: control regret of using an effect estimate bh on the true plant b -----------------
   static causal control: action u moves x = b*u; cost to reach target xt with effort r. */
cost(u, bb) := (bb*u - xt)^2 + rr*u^2$
ustar(bb)  := xt*bb/(bb^2 + rr)$
regret(bh, b) := ratsimp(cost(ustar(bh), b) - cost(ustar(b), b))$

/* causal control uses bh = b (the interventional effect) -> exactly zero regret */
print("Part 2  causal regret  = regret(b, b) =", regret(b, b), "  (interventional cost -> oracle)")$

/* predictive control uses bh = b_obs = b + beta -> a positive floor, function of beta only (no n) */
reg_pred : ratsimp(regret(b + beta_s, b))$          /* beta_s := the fixed bias, abstract */
print("Part 2  predictive regret = regret(b+beta,b) =", reg_pred)$
print("Part 2  at beta=0:", ratsimp(subst(beta_s = 0, reg_pred)), "  (no confounding -> no gap)")$
lead : ratsimp(coeff(expand(taylor(regret(b + beta_s, b), beta_s, 0, 2)), beta_s, 2))$
print("Part 2  predictive regret ~ C*beta^2, C =", lead, " > 0  (floor grows with confounding, fixed in n)")$

/* ---- Part 3: the separation. Predictive regret is bounded BELOW away from zero; causal is zero. */
print("Part 3  predictive floor = C*beta^2 > 0 iff beta != 0 (confounding present);")$
print("        causal regret = 0. Gap does NOT close with more data -- only causal identification closes it.")$
